From 6482595d38c94798f2d116eb6e5a9ff5a1370a12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:34:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(gcode): read a first slice of HEIDENHAIN Klartext
 (.H) programs

Add parse_klartext / parse_klartext_with in camcraft-gcode. The reader
gives the same ParsedProgram sections as the RS-274 reader. It reads
BEGIN/END PGM, BLK FORM, TOOL CALL (number or name), L with FMAX and
modal F, CC + C, CR, CT, CYCL DEF 247 and the drilling cycles 200, 203
and 205 (CYCL CALL, M99), literal Q parameters, M140 MB and the common
M functions. It refuses every other function by name, with the line and
the block number. ParsedSection gets a tool_name field for named tools.

Pinned by the klartext test binary: a round trip of the recorded
Klartext post golden against its CL stream, path, cycle and refusal
tests, and degenerate-input tests (all truncations, bad numbers, 200k
blocks, seeded mutations).

Refs #2227

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
